{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01LqkDk6soo3MbMdSFMgzY39","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01He1irrf55Fr3dTv7zPWSob","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr edit 41 --repo har-ki/claude-code-sre-handbook --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Trigger\n- **When:** 2026-05-19T18:42:15.446667+00:00\n- **Window:** 1-minute lookback\n- **Error rate at trigger:** 19%\n- **Samples in window:** 272\n- **Threshold:** 15%\n\n## Investigation\n\n### Summary\n\nA TOCTOU (time-of-check/time-of-use) race condition in `inventory.js:reserveInventory()` caused the in-memory stock counter for product 7 (Ceramic Plant Pot) to be over-decremented to **-3**, permanently blocking all subsequent checkouts for that product. The error is isolated to `POST /api/checkout`; no other endpoints are affected and the pod is healthy.\n\n### Error rate\n\n| Window | Total log entries | ERROR entries | Rate |\n|--------|-------------------|---------------|------|\n| Last 15 min | 700 | 136 | **19.4%** |\n\nThe 19% trigger rate and the 19.4% observed rate are consistent — the watcher fired ~90 seconds after errors began, so the 1-minute trigger window captured the early burst; the 15-minute window includes the full sustained stream.\n\n### Timeline\n\n- `2026-05-19 18:41:04.401` — **First race fired**: `Inventory inconsistency: stock for product 7 (Ceramic Plant Pot) is -1 after decrement (was 5 at read time)` (TraceId: `8b7eab197db1912a779d3f0200ceaa15`)\n- `2026-05-19 18:41:04.411` — **Second race fired** (10 ms later): stock driven to -3 (TraceId: `ed1ac547bf43f4c04a847c31ae76aab7`)\n- `2026-05-19 18:41:14` onward — All checkout attempts for product 7 fail with: `Insufficient stock for product 7 (Ceramic Plant Pot): requested 2, available -3`\n- Sustained rate: ~52 errors/minute through the observation window\n\n### Root cause — TOCTOU race in `inventory.js`\n\nFile: `otel-demo/ecommerce/backend/src/services/inventory.js`\n\n```\nLine 39:  const currentStock = await getStock(item.id);   // 5 ms simulated DB read\nLines 42–49: if (currentStock < item.quantity) throw ...  // check passes: 5 >= 2\nLines 52–53: await new Promise(resolve =>                  // ← 50–150 ms window\n               setTimeout(resolve, 50 + Math.random() * 100));\nLine 55:  inventory[item.id] -= item.quantity;             // decrement applied\n```\n\nWith multiple concurrent requests all landing during the 50–150 ms \"business rules\" delay:\n\n1. Req-A reads `stock=5` → passes check → waits\n2. Req-B reads `stock=5` → passes check → waits  (concurrently, during Req-A's wait)\n3. Req-C reads `stock=5` → passes check → waits  (concurrently)\n4. Req-A decrements: `5 − 2 = 3` ✓\n5. Req-B decrements: `3 − 2 = 1` ✓\n6. Req-C decrements: `1 − 2 = -1` → `StockMismatchError` emitted, but **stock remains at -1**\n7. Req-D decrements: `-1 − 2 = -3` → `StockMismatchError`; stock now permanently **-3**\n\nAll subsequent reads via `getStock()` return `-3`; every checkout for product 7 fails the `currentStock < item.quantity` guard (`-3 < 2`), returning HTTP 409.\n\nThe `StockMismatchError` branch at lines 58–85 logs the inconsistency and throws, but **does not roll back the decrement**, so the corruption is permanent for the lifetime of the process.\n\n### Kubernetes pod health\n\n```\nNAME                             READY   RESTARTS   AGE     STATUS\necommerce-api-7c7f4fd679-mxsx4   1/1     0          ~2 min  Running\n```\n\n- No restarts, no OOM kills, no evictions.\n- Pod started at `18:40:43` — approximately 21 seconds before the first race fired.\n- QoS class: `BestEffort` (no resource limits set); no resource pressure observed.\n- The load-generator pods show 2 restarts on one replica, consistent with the load burst that triggered the race.\n\n### Log evidence (representative sample)\n\n```\n18:41:04.401  ERROR  Inventory inconsistency: stock for product 7 (Ceramic Plant Pot) is -1 after decrement (was 5 at read time)\n18:41:04.411  ERROR  Inventory inconsistency: stock for product 7 (Ceramic Plant Pot) is -3 after decrement (was 5 at read time)\n18:41:14.069  ERROR  Checkout failed: order=ORD-BF98B010 — Insufficient stock for product 7 (Ceramic Plant Pot): requested 2, available -3\n18:42:18.226  ERROR  Checkout failed: order=ORD-D49113AF — Insufficient stock for product 7 (Ceramic Plant Pot): requested 2, available -3\n18:42:36.848  ERROR  Checkout failed: order=ORD-6D5BEC13 — Insufficient stock for product 7 (Ceramic Plant Pot): requested 2, available -3\n```\n\nAll 136 errors share a single error class. No payment service errors, no other products affected.\n\n### Confidence\n\n**High.** The race condition is directly observable in the `StockMismatchError` log entries, which record both the pre-read value (`was 5 at read time`) and the post-decrement value (`is -3`). The 50–150 ms async gap in `reserveInventory()` (line 53) is the exact window required. No ambiguity about the affected component or code path.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\nAdded a synchronous re-read of `inventory[item.id]` immediately before the decrement in `reserveInventory` (`otel-demo/ecommerce/backend/src/services/inventory.js`). Because there is no `await` between the re-read and the write, Node.js's single-threaded event loop guarantees these two operations are atomic — no other request can interleave during this check-then-act. If the re-read reveals insufficient stock (i.e., another concurrent request decremented during the processing delay), an error is thrown before any write occurs, preventing stock from going negative.\n\nCommit: `e66e699f` (`fix(inventory): prevent TOCTOU race in reserveInventory`)\n\nIncident report: [`docs/incidents/2026-05-19-6e14cf73.md`](docs/incidents/2026-05-19-6e14cf73.md)\n\n## Incident report\n\n`docs/incidents/2026-05-19-6e14cf73.md`\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1","description":"Update PR #41 body with proposed fix and incident report sections"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"s